    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's a good start. some people try to argue that we should just retrain workers or focus on new types of jobs instead, but that feels like a totally unrealistic response to the sheer scale of what's coming. could you explain why those traditional \"retraining\" arguments are basically obsolete compared to UBI?",
